            <div xml:id="d94">

                <pb facs="0099" n="93" xml:id="pg93"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.102S/1908: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-10-09T14:00:00+08:00">October 9, 1939—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 9—8:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>902. Reference my 893, October 6, 10 a.m. I have today replied to British Consul
                    General that I have submitted his letter for the consideration of the
                    Commander-in-Chief and conferred with him on the existing situation, and that it
                    is considered inadvisable to adopt the proposed measure at this time.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Chungking, Peiping, Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
